---
<section class="app-section">
  <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
  <h2>Every approaching car, with its speed.</h2>
  <ul class="features">
    <li>
      <h3>Live radar field</h3>
      <p>Vehicles appear at the top of the screen and glide down toward you, each labelled with its speed as it closes in.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Peak speed, kept</h3>
      <p>The most trustworthy reading is the one taken far away, so each vehicle keeps its top speed. Recent vehicles stay in a strip along the bottom.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Best standing still</h3>
      <p>Set the radar at the roadside, aimed up the road. When the radar isn&rsquo;t moving, what it measures is the vehicle&rsquo;s real speed.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Works with Garmin Varia</h3>
      <p>Pairs with the Varia RTL515 and RCT715. Speeds show in mph or km/h, following your iPhone&rsquo;s region.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="app-section">
  <p class="eyebrow">Free and private</p>
  <h2>A free utility for everyone.</h2>
  <ul class="features">
    <li>
      <h3>No account</h3>
      <p>No sign-up and no login. Pair your radar once and it reconnects on its own.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Nothing leaves your phone</h3>
      <p>Acme Radar talks to your radar over Bluetooth and nothing else. It has no servers, no ads, and no tracking.</p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <h3>Not a radar gun</h3>
      <p>The speeds are for curiosity and traffic awareness. The radar reports to the nearest 1&nbsp;km/h, and its readings aren&rsquo;t certified for enforcement.</p>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
